  "verdict": "In the production convention the ToA-aligning DM = 272.5528 pc/cm^-3 lands on the DSA DM-phase optimum (0.10 sigma) and is 7.2 sigma below the CHIME/joint optimum. The observed CHIME-DSA offset (-4.97 ms) vs geometric (-2.28 ms) discrepancy is therefore explained by the CHIME-DSA DM difference (+0.0773 pc/cm^-3): adopting the lower DSA DM reduces the ToA residual to 0.21 ms (well within the 2.4 ms combined error). The offset does NOT require a DM outside the measured band; it is consistent with DSA-DM adoption for the geometric reference, while the manuscript's chime_primary catalog adoption leaves a ~2.0 ms (0.85x combined-error) residual."
